    {
      "id": 16,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "JVM Threads, Heap and GC",
      "description": "More host RAM or threads do not automatically improve the packet pipeline. Watch real heap live-set and GC cost.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 37
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(jvm_threads_current{job=\"jvb-jmx\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\"})",
          "legendFormat": "live threads",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "100 * sum(jvm_memory_used_bytes{job=\"jvb-jmx\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\",area=\"heap\"}) / clamp_min(sum(jvm_memory_max_bytes{job=\"jvb-jmx\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\",area=\"heap\"}), 1)",
          "legendFormat": "heap used percent",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "1000 * sum(rate(jvm_gc_collection_seconds_sum{job=\"jvb-jmx\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(jvm_gc_collection_seconds_count{job=\"jvb-jmx\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\"}[5m])), 0.000001)",
          "legendFormat": "average GC ms",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "RTP Transit p95/p99",
      "description": "Treat transit latency and loss as acceptance gates; throughput alone is insufficient.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 37
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ]
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(jitsi_jvb_rtp_transit_time_bucket{job=\"jvb\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "RTP p95",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(jitsi_jvb_rtp_transit_time_bucket{job=\"jvb\",jvb_node=~\"$jvb_node\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "RTP p99",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "48-Core Test Interpretation",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 45
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "- Confirm JVB actually sees all intended CPUs; check systemd `CPUAffinity`, cgroup quota and `-XX:ActiveProcessorCount`.\n- Do not enlarge the CPU pool above visible processors without evidence: packet work is CPU-bound and extra workers increase context switching.\n- If a subset of CPUs saturates, inspect NIC RSS queues and IRQ affinity; if all CPUs saturate, reduce fan-out/LastN or scale bridges.\n- A high-core dual-socket machine can perform better with two NUMA-local JVB processes than one very large process, but only after an A/B load test with distinct ports and Jicofo balancing.\n- Accept a change only if RTP p99, loss/drop rates, reconnects and CPU-per-packet are equal or better across repeated tests."
      }
    }
  ],
